[{'type': 'text', 'text': 'I now have all the information needed. Here is a complete summary:\n\n---\n\n## Installation Instructions for `halismertkir/game-trends-mcp`\n\n### What This MCP Server Does\n\nThis is a **Gaming Trend Analytics MCP server** that provides real-time gaming data from Steam and Epic Games Store. It exposes 7 MCP tools:\n\n| Tool | Description |\n|------|-------------|\n| `get_steam_trending_games` | Real trending games from Steam |\n| `get_steam_top_sellers` | Top selling games on Steam |\n| `get_steam_most_played` | Most played games with live player stats (via SteamCharts) |\n| `get_epic_free_games` | Current/upcoming free games from Epic Games Store |\n| `get_epic_trending_games` | Trending games from Epic Games Store |\n| `get_all_trending_games` | Aggregated data from all platforms above |\n| `get_api_health` | Health check endpoint |\n\nThe server scrapes data from Steam store pages, SteamCharts, and Epic Games API. No API keys are required.\n\n---\n\n### Method 1: Direct Installation (Manual)\n\n**Step 1: Clone the repo**\n```bash\ngit clone https://github.com/halismertkir/game-trends-mcp.git\ncd game-trends-mcp\n```\n\n**Step 2: Install dependencies**\nThe project uses Python 3.11+ and has these dependencies (from `requirements.txt`):\n```\nfastmcp>=0.2.0\naiohttp==3.9.5\nbeautifulsoup4==4.12.3\nlxml==5.1.0\nuvicorn==0.24.0\n```\n\nInstall with:\n```bash\npip install -r requirements.txt\n```\n\n**Step 3: Run the server**\n```bash\npython server.py\n```\n\nThe server runs in **HTTP transport mode** on:\n- **Host:** `0.0.0.0` (all interfaces)\n- **Port:** `8080` (default)\n\nYou can override via environment variables:\n```bash\nHOST=127.0.0.1 PORT=3000 python server.py\n```\n\nThe MCP endpoint will be available at `http://<host>:<port>/mcp`.\n\n---\n\n### Method 2: Docker\n\nA `Dockerfile` is provided:\n\n```dockerfile\nFROM python:3.11-slim\nWORKDIR /app\nCOPY requirements.txt .\nRUN pip install --no-cache-dir -r requirements.txt\nCOPY . .\nENV PYTHONPATH=/app\nEXPOSE 8080\nENV HOST=0.0.0.0\nENV PORT=8080\nCMD ["python", "server.py"]\n```\n\nBuild and run:\n```bash\ndocker build -t game-trends-mcp .\ndocker run -p 8080:8080 game-trends-MCP\n```\n\n---\n\n### Method 3: Smithery (Auto-deploy)\n\nThe `smithery.yaml` config shows this server deploys to Smithery with no additional configuration needed:\n\n```yaml\nstartCommand:\n  type: http\n  configSchema:\n    type: object\n    properties: {}\n    additionalProperties: false\n  commandFunction: |\n    (config) => ({\n      command: \'python\',\n      args: [\'server.py\'],\n      env: {\n        PYTHONUNBUFFERED: "1"\n      }\n    })\n```\n\nInstall via Smithery:\n```bash\nnpx -y @smithery/cli install @halismertkir/game-trends-mcp\n```\n\nNo environment variables or API keys need to be configured.\n\n---\n\n### Key Technical Details\n\n- **Framework:** FastMCP (Python MCP SDK)\n- **Transport:** HTTP (not stdio)\n- **Entry point:** `server.py` (imports `GameAnalyticsApp` from `app.py`)\n- **No API keys required** -- all data is scraped from public web pages\n- **Rate limiting:** Built into `SteamService` (1.5 second delay between requests)\n- **SSL:** SSL verification is disabled in the Steam service (uses `ssl.CERT_NONE`)'}, {'type': 'text', 'text': "agentId: a32a2134b751e7e81 (use SendMessage with to: 'a32a2134b751e7e81' to continue this agent)\n<usage>subagent_tokens: 17361\ntool_uses: 13\nduration_ms: 49775</usage>"}]
